  "title": "Build a Complete Titan LBO Model: Entry to Exit Returns",
  "scenario": "Titan Company Limited is under consideration for acquisition by a PE consortium. The fund has estimated an entry EV of ₹60,000 Cr (10x FY26 EBITDA of ₹6,000 Cr) and must model five years of operations, debt amortisation, and exit returns to validate whether the deal clears the fund's 20% IRR hurdle. You will construct the full LBO model: Sources & Uses (entry capital structure), operating assumptions, a five-year debt schedule (showing how cash flow deleverages), and the final returns calculation (MOIC and IRR).",
  "instructions": "Build a complete LBO model for Titan by: (1) verifying Sources equal Uses; (2) calculating the Sponsor Equity stake percentage; (3) projecting Year-5 exit enterprise value; (4) computing exit equity after debt repayment; (5) calculating the money multiple (MOIC); and (6) deriving the IRR. Use the data and assumptions provided to fill in the Answers sheet formulas.",
  "learning_objective": "Construct a full leveraged buyout model end-to-end — from entry capital structure through debt amortisation to exit valuation — and compute IRR and MOIC to assess deal returns against a 20% hurdle rate.",
  "hints": [
    "For Sources & Uses balance: total all debt and equity sources, then compare to total uses (purchase EV + fees). They must match exactly.",
    "Sponsor Equity is the 'plug' — calculate it as Total Uses minus all other sources (debt, mezzanine, rollover equity, management options, cash on hand).",
    "Year-5 EBITDA grows from ₹6,000 Cr at 9.6% CAGR annually. Apply the growth rate iteratively or use a compound growth formula (FV = PV × (1 + rate)^periods)."
  ],
